# When the Saints — the traditional tune (public domain) played by one horn note from "The Thunderer",
# pitched to each note of the melody, over a tuba that follows the chords and the march's own drums.
# Open it in the Melodies tab to see the tune on the piano roll.

tempo 116
key F major
samples ../samples

clip horn   = marine-band/stems/Thunderer/other.wav  shot-7
clip tuba   = marine-band/stems/WashingtonPost/bass.wav  pick 1bar
clip groove = marine-band/stems/Thunderer/drums.wav  loop-1  warp beats

# a pickup bar, then the 15-bar tune
chords I | I | I | I | I | I | I | V7 | V7 | I | I7 | IV | IV | I | V7 | I

# Oh when the saints | go marching in | oh when the saints go marching in | oh Lord I want to be in that number | when the saints go marching in
track horn    notes ". 1 3 4 | 5 _ _ _ | . 1 3 4 | 5 _ _ _ | . 1 3 4 | 5 _ 3 _ | 1 _ 3 _ | 2 _ _ _ | . 3 _ 2 | 1 _ 1 3 | 5 _ 5 _ | 4 _ _ _ | . 3 4 5 | 3 _ 1 _ | 2 _ _ _ | 1 _ _ _"  grid 4
track tuba    follow  volume -4
track groove  transpose 0  volume -6
